    <!-- About -->
    <string name="about_title">About</string>
    <string name="about_version">Seenly · version %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_intro">Translation and text recognition for images, screenshots and camera photos. An open-source Kotlin Multiplatform project.</string>
    <string name="about_unofficial">Unofficial app</string>
    <string name="about_unofficial_1">This is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed or supported by Google LLC. Google, Google Lens and Google Translate are trademarks of Google LLC; they are named here only to describe which services the app works with.</string>
    <string name="about_unofficial_2">Recognition, translation and search are done by Google services and the other translators you turned on. How they work, whether they are available and their terms do not depend on this app and may change at any time.</string>
    <string name="about_data">What is sent where</string>
    <string name="about_data_1">• The image you open or take is sent to Google Lens for recognition and translation.</string>
    <string name="about_data_2">• Text you translate on its own goes to the translator you chose.</string>
    <string name="about_data_3">• Search results open in your browser, with its own cookies and settings.</string>
    <string name="about_data_4">• History is stored only on this device; the app has no servers or analytics of its own.</string>
    <string name="about_data_5">• The Seenly accessibility service (if you turned it on) does not read windows or watch what you do: it only draws the screen translation over other apps.</string>
    <string name="about_data_6">• Don’t open anything here that you aren’t ready to share with these services.</string>
    <string name="about_source">Source code and licences</string>
    <string name="about_author">Author: bropines. The app uses open-source libraries; their licences are below.</string>
    <string name="about_licences_button">Open-source licences</string>
